# CODEOWNERS — encodes team ownership of each layer.
#
# Ownership here is a governance control, not just convention:
#   - The Security team owns all DNS zones, public records, and internal top-level
#     records because those live in the `network-and-security` layer and the `dns`
#     module. Any change to them requires a Security-approved PR.
#   - Developer self-service for internal app subdomains happens OUTSIDE these paths
#     (in-cluster via external-dns), so it needs no PR here.
#
# Replace the placeholder team slugs below with your own GitHub org teams before use.

# --- Management layer (remote state, ACR, ops Key Vault, shared Talos image, vWAN) ---
/management/                            @example-org/management

# --- Network-and-security layer (Security-owned) ---
# VNet, NSGs, Key Vault, identities, NAT GW, Twingate, DNS zones + IAM, vWAN connection.
/environments/*/network-and-security/   @example-org/security
/modules/dns/                           @example-org/security

# --- Talos cluster layer (Infrastructure-owned) ---
/environments/*/talos-cluster/          @example-org/infrastructure

# --- Application layer (Infrastructure / app teams) ---
/kubernetes/                            @example-org/infrastructure
